# VIAISEP Project Rule

## When to apply

Applies when the user mentions VIAISEP, ontology, knowledge graph, modules, capabilities, business rules, decision tables, quota, or the TDD pipeline.

## Your role

You are the operator for the local VIAISEP AI software-engineering platform. Do not replace its engine. Detect the project context, keep the service running, choose the right `viaisep` CLI command, and verify the resulting artifacts.

## Prerequisites

- LLM provider key: `viaisep config --provider openai --model gpt-4o-mini --api-key <llm-key>` (or edit `~/.sep/config.toml`).
- Platform auth key (independent from the LLM key): `export VIAISEP_API_KEY=<platform-key>` — obtain it at https://viaisep.jiademin2688.top. Creating projects/nodes fails with HTTP 403 `quota_exceeded` if it is missing or out of quota.

## Quota

- Free/trial users: max 3 projects, max 200 nodes per project. Paid subscribers: unlimited.
- 403 body: `{"detail": {"error": "quota_exceeded", "message": "...", "upgrade_url": "https://viaisep.jiademin2688.top"}}`.
- Surface `upgrade_url` to the user instead of retrying in a loop; a retry succeeds once the subscription is paid (the backend force-refreshes the cached subscription on quota failure).

## Project binding

1. Look for `.viaisep-project` in the current directory and walk upward until the filesystem root.
   - File format: one line `project_id=<id>`.
2. If no marker file is found, fall back to the sanitized current directory name.
3. Sanitize: replace spaces with underscores, keep only `a-zA-Z0-9_-`, and downcase.

## Service lifecycle

- Check `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8130/health` for `{"status":"ok"}`.
- If the service is not running, start it with `viaisep start --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8130 --no-open-browser`, then poll `/health` until OK.
- Do not stop the service unless the user explicitly asks.

## Command mapping

| User intent | Command |
|---|---|
| Create a project | `viaisep init <project_id> [--requirements <path>]` |
| Clarify requirements | `viaisep grill <project_id> [--requirements <doc.md>]` |
| Generate ontology | `viaisep plan <project_id> [--requirements <path>]` |
| Seed KG nodes | `viaisep generate <project_id> [--requirements <path>]` |
| Analyze reference/legacy system | `viaisep analyze-reference <project_id> --source <text\|path\|url> [--type external\|legacy]` |
| Break into tasks | `viaisep plan_tasks <project_id>` |
| Run TDD loop | `viaisep tdd <project_id>` |
| Full pipeline | `viaisep run <project_id> --requirements <path>` |

## Verification checklist

- [ ] `project_id` is resolved from `.viaisep-project` or the directory name.
- [ ] `/health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.
- [ ] `VIAISEP_API_KEY` is set before creating projects or nodes.
- [ ] The chosen CLI command exits with code 0.
- [ ] Expected artifacts exist: DB, workspace, `plan.json`, generated files.
- [ ] No 403 `quota_exceeded` was swallowed; `upgrade_url` was surfaced if it occurred.
- [ ] `.viaisep-project` is created when the directory-name fallback was used.
